# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 1: METADATA BLOCK
# ( OmniCode Lexicon Emergence Manifest & AI-Driven Language Proposal Charter )
# ==============================================================================
# ARCHITECTURAL PURPOSE:
#   This directory serves as the project-wide incubation chamber for legal keyword,
#   operator, and grammatical proposals within OmniCode.
#
# WHY THE AI CAN EXPAND THE LEXICON IN A LOCAL INSTANCE:
#   Unlike conventional compiled languages (C, Rust, Python) where keywords and
#   operators are hardcoded into static compiler syntax trees, OmniCode is
#   ontologically grounded and homoiconic:
#   1. Every keyword and operator is defined as a first-class declarative document
#      in the Lexicon (<TRACK 2>/lexicon/).
#   2. The Lexicon engine dynamically ingests these definitions, maps their
#      parts of speech, polarities (+ vs -), boundary ranks, and machine effects.
#   3. The OmniAssembler lowers them into concrete 64-bit balanced-ternary machine
#      words (Word64) and verifies delimiter stack integrity via OmniDebugger.
#   4. An AI running in a local instance can formulate emergent, domain-specific
#      keywords to build a bare-metal OS without hacking the compiler binary.
#
# THE GOLDEN CANONS OF OMNICODE LANGUAGE DESIGN:
#   CANON 1: MORPHEMIC COMPOUNDING
#     If an action can be expressed through natural compounding of base symbols
#     (~ like, ! but, :: and, @ at), it must be an operator (e.g. ::@, ~!).
#
#   CANON 2: UNIVERSAL HUMAN VERBS (ACCESSIBILITY FOR NON-CODERS)
#     If an action requires a verb, choose an everyday human word usable across
#     all domains (OS, Games, UI, AI). Never use developer jargon (spawn, probe, fork).
#     - Use SENSE instead of Probe (every living creature senses its world).
#     - Use AWAKEN instead of Spawn (transitioning from dormancy to active life).
#     - Use PREEMPT instead of Yield/Trap (taking turns with priority).
#     - Use PROVE instead of BIST/Assert (verifying balance before proceeding).
#
#   CANON 3: BOUNDARY TIER DISAMBIGUATION (THE COMPARISON RULE)
#     Because < ... > is the Rank 1 Invariant delimiter, bare `<` and `>` are
#     boundary brackets. All relational comparisons must be cast in context:
#     [ { A } < { B } ]
#     - [ ... ] denotes a concrete evaluation block.
#     - { ... } casts A and B into Context values.
#     - Uncasted `<=>` represents an Invariant of Equivalence (< => >).
# ==============================================================================

Module < Lexicon.Suggestions.Manifest > ( Project-wide lexicon emergence charter ) {
    version: < "1.0.0" >,
    system: < OmniCode.Lexicon.Incubator >,
    semantics: < MorphemicOperators :: UniversalVerbs :: NonCoderAccessibility >
}

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING BLOCK
# ( Incubation Categories, Boundary Ranking Hierarchy & Typology )
# ==============================================================================
Opening {
    requires: [
        Rank1_Invariants : "< ... > (Absolute Immutable Laws & Types)" ::
        Rank2_Denotations : "[ ... ] (Concrete Silicon Evaluation Blocks)" ::
        Rank3_Contexts   : "{ ... } (Environmental Attributes & State Values)" ::
        Rank4_Asides     : "( ... ) (Teleological Intent & Secondary Checks)"
    ],
    preconditions: [ +1 : PROCEED ]
}

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY BLOCK
# ( Incubation Registry & Proposal Manifests )
# ==============================================================================
Body [
    # Proposal 1: Morphological Symbolic Operators (operators/morphological_operators.omni)
    proposal_operators [
        SituatedAt_Binding  [ "::@" [ ChannelBind & AddressOffset ] ] ::
        CaveatInterrupt_Hop [ "~!"  [ ApproximateLike & InvariantCaveat ] ] ::
        ContextComparison   [ "[ { A } < { B } ]" [ CastedContextRelation ] ] ::
        InvariantBalance    [ "<=>" [ InvariantEquivalenceState ] ]
    ] ( Symbolic operator proposals compounding from atomic morphemes )

    # Proposal 2: Universal Human Verbs (03_verbs/universal_verbs.omni)
    proposal_verbs [
        Verb_Preempt [ "PREEMPT" [ PriorityInterruption & TaskTurnTaking ] ] ::
        Verb_Sense   [ "SENSE"   [ EnvironmentalDiscovery & HardwarePerception ] ] ::
        Verb_Awaken  [ "AWAKEN"  [ ColdStartInception & ProcessActivation ] ] ::
        Verb_Prove   [ "PROVE"   [ BalancedTernarySelfTest & InvariantValidation ] ]
    ] ( Universal human verbs replacing developer jargon )
]

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: CLOSING BLOCK
# ( Tripartite Consensus & Covenant Sealing )
# ==============================================================================
Closing {
    verify: [
        proposal_operators = yes ::
        proposal_verbs = yes
    ],
    commit_status [ PROCEED ] ( Suggestion incubator sealed and active )
}
